2026-09-17 02:54:18,116 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=adjudication data={"argument_id": "1ec12115-e02e-4848-ba36-f3e59f87da1e", "created_at": "2026-09-17T00:54:17.987458", "failure_effects": ["V has formally presented a prioritized, concrete, verifiable demand list (welfare, housing, equality, reduced profit-seeking) in the C+S+MP working group, signaling phased reform introduction and flexibility on secondary issues.", "V confirms that its decisive abstention and budget support are conditional on a verifiable package and credible budget path; this conditional commitment stands regardless of the roll.", "The working group remains deadlocked: C's liberal-economy/school/decentralization demands continue to conflict irreconcilably with V's welfare/equality demands and MP's binding climate commitments within a single credible fiscal framework; no concrete verifiable package is finalized, and the PM vote and budget majority remain unsecured."], "mode": "probabilistic", "probability": 0.35, "rationale": "Authority gate: V can credibly present its own prioritized demand list and condition its own abstention/budget support on a verifiable package; that self-binding declaration is feasible. However, the Desired Effect's core outcome\u2014the C+S+MP working group finalizing a concrete verifiable package that balances C's liberal priorities, V's core demands, and MP's binding climate commitments within one credible fiscal framework, thereby securing the PM vote (NO<175) and budget majority (176)\u2014depends on other actors' commitments. Active Effects 38a38dac and 5fc537a4 authoritatively establish that the working group is deadlocked precisely on this irreconcilable core conflict, with C withholding JA/AVSTAR and V withholding tolerance. V's action does not create C's or MP's acceptance; it only restates V's own conditional position. The hidden information confirms C's high credibility cost for breaking its public no, and that C requires verifiable policy exc